From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gdiplus: a font family found by a name mapped to it

GdipCreateFontFamilyFromName enumerates the name with GDI and looks the
result up among the installed families -- by the font's full name, which
carries its style ("Inter Regular", "Carlito Regular"). A name Wine maps to
such a font (Fonts\Replacements: Tahoma, Microsoft Sans Serif and Segoe UI
to Inter, Calibri to Carlito) was FontFamilyNotFound, and .NET programs that
make a Font of it failed in their type initializers (AmbirScan's GdPicture,
David 2026-10-02). The family is the longest one the full name begins with,
word for word, when none is the full name itself.

Test: test/gdipfamily-gate.sh (mutant GDIP_FULLNAME_ONLY).
---
--- a/dlls/gdiplus/font.c
+++ b/dlls/gdiplus/font.c
@@ -724,14 +724,38 @@
 
     if (!EnumFontFamiliesW(hdc, name, is_font_installed_proc, (LPARAM)&lf))
     {
+        int best = -1;
+        size_t best_len = 0;
+
         for (i = 0; i < collection->count; i++)
         {
-            if (!wcsicmp(lf.lfFaceName, collection->FontFamilies[i]->FamilyName))
+            const WCHAR *fam = collection->FontFamilies[i]->FamilyName;
+            size_t len = wcslen(fam);
+
+            if (!wcsicmp(lf.lfFaceName, fam))
             {
-                status = GdipCloneFontFamily(collection->FontFamilies[i], family);
-                TRACE("<-- %p\n", *family);
+                best = i;
                 break;
             }
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_GDIP_FULLNAME_ONLY
+            /* Stained Glass OS: the name is the font's full name, which
+             * carries its style ("Inter Regular", "Carlito Regular") -- not
+             * its family's: Tahoma, Microsoft Sans Serif and Segoe UI (Inter
+             * here) and Calibri (Carlito) were "not found", and .NET
+             * programs failed in their type initializers (AmbirScan's
+             * GdPicture, David 2026-10-02). The longest family the full name
+             * begins with, word for word. */
+            if (len > best_len && !wcsnicmp(lf.lfFaceName, fam, len) && lf.lfFaceName[len] == ' ')
+            {
+                best = i;
+                best_len = len;
+            }
+#endif
+        }
+        if (best >= 0)
+        {
+            status = GdipCloneFontFamily(collection->FontFamilies[best], family);
+            TRACE("<-- %p\n", *family);
         }
     }
 
